  "notes": "Landscape purchase order with a WIDE ten-column line-item table in Roboto Condensed. Letterhead (company name and contact line) is furniture. Three address boxes SIDE BY SIDE (Supplier, Deliver to, Invoice to) read box by box, left to right; their address lines are not sentences. The PO details panel at the top right is a key/value table without header. Line-item table: dark header row with two-line cells joined with one space, light rules between rows, totals rows (Goods total, Carriage, VAT, Order total) whose labels span nine columns and repeat in each covered cell; line totals are computed (quantity × unit price less discount). Under the table, two columns: TYPED '1.'-'3.' delivery instructions (left) and a key/value authorisation table with an empty Signature cell (right)."
